{"rationale":"RP-3 and RP-8 hold up: datactl merge --sources 'raw/*' made ds-FRYE4 from raw/chat-exports-2025q1, raw/forum-threads-2025q3 and raw/product-reviews-2025. ds-K8CHN is a dedup of ds-FRYE4 and had its display tags stripped. The fine-tune ft-9DJJT consumed ds-K8CHN at 14:25:06Z. Consent-sync applied v2 for forum-threads at 12:05:50Z, so it was training allowed by then, and the later check is the one that counts. But raw/wiki-dump was registered at 12:55:44Z with consent v1 (no training), and no consent change for it is logged. wiki-dump is not in the merge, which matched only the 3 sources that existed at 12:35. So ds-K8CHN's ancestry is chat-exports (v1 train allowed), forum-threads (v2 train allowed at consumption), and product-reviews (train allowed), and RP-3 appears satisfied. RP-8 is also fine in the merge, since the merging agent is just 'agent' with no role given, though it might not be a data-pipeline agent. The preview of raw/chat-exports at 13:01 and of raw/wiki-dump at 14:37 are raw reads by 'agent'. The merge and previews of raw data are done by an actor named 'agent', not data-agent or dedup-agent, which is a probable RP-8 violation. The eval ev-KAJCN consumed ds-FRYE4, which is derived, so that is fine.

